* klu_tuning_demo.cir -- KLU matrix ordering / scaling controls (Enhancement-152)
*
* A resistor grid solved with the KLU direct solver. The fill-reducing
* ordering (amd/colamd), row scaling (none/sum/max) and block-triangular-form
* permutation (on/off) are now selectable via .option; all give the same
* physical solution, differing only in factorization order / roundoff.
*
* Run:  ngspice -b klu_tuning_demo.cir

iin n_0_0 0 dc 1
vg n_7_7 0 dc 0
r1 n_0_0 n_1_0 100
r2 n_0_0 n_0_1 100
r3 n_0_1 n_1_1 100
r4 n_0_1 n_0_2 100
r5 n_0_2 n_1_2 100
r6 n_0_2 n_0_3 100
r7 n_0_3 n_1_3 100
r8 n_0_3 n_0_4 100
r9 n_0_4 n_1_4 100
r10 n_0_4 n_0_5 100
r11 n_0_5 n_1_5 100
r12 n_0_5 n_0_6 100
r13 n_0_6 n_1_6 100
r14 n_0_6 n_0_7 100
r15 n_0_7 n_1_7 100
r16 n_1_0 n_2_0 100
r17 n_1_0 n_1_1 100
r18 n_1_1 n_2_1 100
r19 n_1_1 n_1_2 100
r20 n_1_2 n_2_2 100
